Moment shadow versus compatibility wall
HYP-2530 / T822 / OPEN-Q-101 candidate

[1] Exhaustive n=6 baby-Hodge holes and convex spectral certificates
  hole (c3,c5)=(5,3) = 1/2*(5,2) + 1/2*(5,4)
    lower witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 5) H=15 D=0 bits=140
    upper witness: score=(1, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4) H=19 D=0 bits=20
  hole (c3,c5)=(5,5) = 1/2*(5,4) + 1/2*(5,6)
    lower witness: score=(1, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4) H=19 D=0 bits=20
    upper witness: score=(1, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4) H=27 D=1 bits=80
  hole (c3,c5)=(7,8) = 1/2*(7,7) + 1/2*(7,9)
    lower witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 4) H=37 D=2 bits=152
    upper witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 4) H=33 D=0 bits=88
  hole (c3,c5)=(8,7) = 1/2*(8,6) + 1/2*(8,8)
    lower witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3) H=45 D=4 bits=408
    upper witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3) H=41 D=2 bits=280
  hole (c3,c5)=(8,9) = 2/3*(8,8) + 1/3*(8,11)
    lower witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3) H=41 D=2 bits=280
    upper witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3) H=43 D=1 bits=344
  hole (c3,c5)=(8,10) = 1/3*(8,8) + 2/3*(8,11)
    lower witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3) H=41 D=2 bits=280
    upper witness: score=(2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3) H=43 D=1 bits=344

  Flagship hole:
    (c3,c5)=(8,10) is spectrally moment-interior: it sits in the same
    c3-fiber between realized points (8,8) and (8,11).
    Therefore the one-particle spectral/moment shadow permits it; the
    obstruction must live in the compatibility/conflict layer (THM-499 D).

[2] Odd Faulhaber moments as a Stieltjes cone
  Exact identity: S_{2r+1}(n) = sum_{i=1..n} i*(i^2)^r
  So the odd-moment Hankel matrices are PSD; leading determinants are:
    n=1: leading Hankel determinants [1, 0, 0, 0]
    n=2: leading Hankel determinants [3, 18, 0, 0]
    n=3: leading Hankel determinants [6, 360, 86400, 0]
    n=4: leading Hankel determinants [10, 3000, 15120000, 548674560000]
    n=5: leading Hankel determinants [15, 15750, 740880000, 967861923840000]
    n=6: leading Hankel determinants [21, 61740, 17425497600, 341461686730752000]
  Interpretation: the odd-moment lane already lives in a positive moment cone;
  the failure of exact p>=3 towers is again beyond positivity, at the
  Bernoulli/integrality/compatibility layer.

[3] Cross-thread synthesis
  Tournament side: c5=10 is a baby-Hodge hole that survives the simplest
  moment/convex relaxation.
  Faulhaber side: odd moments satisfy exact Hankel positivity automatically.
  Shared lesson: moment positivity is only the one-particle shadow.
  Real obstructions are packet/compatibility/integrality constraints.

